{
  "title": "6: al-An'aam الأنعام",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَجَعَلَ الظُّلُمٰتِ وَالنُّوْرَ  ؕ ثُمَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(1)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ZOLOMAATE WAALNNOORA SUMMA LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM YAA’DELOONA.\nAll praise is God’s, Who created the heavens and the earth and caused the darkness and the light; yet those who disbelieve set up equals with their Lord.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ ثُمَّ قَضٰۤى اَجَلًا  ؕ وَاَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّى عِنْدَهٗ ثُمَّ اَنْتُمْ تَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(2)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN TEENIN SUMMA QAZAA AAJALAN WA AJALUM AJALIM I’NDAHU SUMMA ANTUM TAMTAROON.\nHe it is Who Created you of clay, then decreed the term (of your life); and the term determined is with Him and yet ye doubt (thereof).\nوَهُوَ اللّٰهُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَفِى الْاَرْضِؕ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّكُمْ وَ جَهْرَكُمْ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(3)\nWA HOWA LAAHO FIL SAMAAWAATE WA ARZ YA’LAMO SERRAKUM WA JAHRAKUM YA’LAMO MAA TAKSEBOONA.\nAnd He is God in the heavens and in the earth! He knoweth your secrets and your disclosures! and He knoweth what ye earn (for yourselves by your deeds).\nوَمَا تَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ مِّنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(4)\nWA MAA TAA-TEEHIM MIN AAYATIM MIN AAYAATIL RABBEHIM ILLAA KAANOO A’NHAA MOA’REZEEN.\nThere came not unto them any sign from the signs of their Lord but they turned away from it.\nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْؕ فَسَوْفَ يَاْتِيْهِمْ اَنْۢبٰٓؤُا مَا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(5)\nFAQAD KAZZABOO BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAAHUM FA-SAWFA YAATEEHIM AANBAAAUA MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nThey have indeed belied the truth when it came to them; therefore, very soon the tidings will come (be known) to them of what they mocked at.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ مَّكَّنّٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَا لَمْ نُمَكِّنْ لَّكُمْ وَاَرْسَلْنَا السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّجَعَلْنَا الْاَنْهٰرَ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمْ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ وَاَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(6)\nALAM YARAW KAM AHLAKNAL MIN QABLEHIM MIN QARNIN MMAKKANNAAHUM FIL ARZE MAA LAM LAHUM LAKUM WA ARSALNAA SAMAAA-AD A’LAYHIM MMEDRAARAN WA JA-A’LNAA AL-AANHAARA TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEM FA AHLAKNAAHUM BEZUNOOBEHEM WA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QARNAN AAKHEREEN.\nSee they not how many a generation before them We have destroyed, whom We had established in the earth (to the extent to) which We had not yet established you (till now), and We sent the clouds to rain abundantly upon them, and We made the rivers flow beneath (their dwellings) and yea We destroyed them for their sins and raised up after them another generation.\nوَلَوْ نَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ كِتٰبًا فِىْ قِرْطَاسٍ فَلَمَسُوْهُ بِاَيْدِيْهِمْ لَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(7)\nWA LAW NAZZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABAA FEE QERTAASIN FALAMASOOHU BE-AYDEEHIM LAQAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd had We sent down unto thee a book written on a paper, and they had touched it with their hands, surely those who disbelieved had said, “This is naught but obvious sorcery.\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ مَلَكٌ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنْزَلْنَا مَلَكًا لَّقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ ثُمَّ لَا يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE MALAKUN WA LAW ANZALNAA MALAKAN LLAQUZEAAA MIN SUMMA LAA HUM YUNZAROON.\nAnd they say “Why has not an angel been sent down unto him?” And had We sent down an angel the matter would certainly have been decided (once for all) and then they would not have been respited.\nوَلَوْ جَعَلْنٰهُ مَلَكًا لَّجَعَلْنٰهُ رَجُلًا وَّلَلَبَسْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّا يَلْبِسُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA LAW LAW MALAKAN LLAJAA’ALNAAHU RAJULAN WWALALABASNAA A’LAYHIM MAA YALBESOONA.\nAnd had We made him an Angel, We would have certainly made him a man, and We would certainly have made confused to them what they (now) make confused.\nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَحَاقَ بِالَّذِيْنَ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAHAAQA BE-LAZEENA SAKHEROOA MINHUM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd certainly, were mocked (many) apostles before thee but that which they mocked at encompassed the scoffers among them.\nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ انْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(11)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE SUMMA ANZUROOA KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Travel ye in the earth; then see ye what hath been the end of the beliers (of our apostles’).\nقُلْ لِّمَنْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلْ لِّلّٰهِؕ كَتَبَ عَلٰى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ  ؕ لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ ؕ اَلَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(12)\nQUL LEMAN MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QUL LELLAAHE KATABAL A’LAA NAFSEHE AR-RAHMATA LAYAJMAA’ANNAKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEHE LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nSay! “To whom belongeth what is in the heavens and the earth?” Say thou “To God; He hath prescribed mercy on Himself; Most certainly He will gather you on the Resurrection Day, there is no doubt about it; (As for) those who have lost (ruined) their selves, they will not believe.\nوَلَهٗ مَا سَكَنَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِؕ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(13)\nWA LAHU MAA SAKANA FIL LAYLE WA WA WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nAnd to Him belongeth whatever dwelleth in the night and the day; And He is the All-Hearing and the All-Knowing.\nقُلْ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَتَّخِذُ وَلِيًّا فَاطِرِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَهُوَ يُطْعِمُ وَلَا يُطْعَمُؕ قُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ مَنْ اَسْلَمَ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(14)\nQUL AAGHAYRA LAAHE AATTAKHEZU WALIYYANW FAATERE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA HOWA YUTE’EMU WA LAA YUTA’AMU QUL INNEE AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA AWWALA MAN ASLAMA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay, “Shall I take a guardian besides God, the Originator of the heavens and the earth? while He feedeth (others) and is not (Himself) fed Say! “I am commanded to be the first who submitteth himself (to God) ” and be not thou of the polytheists.\nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(15)\nQUL INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nSay! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Verily I fear should I disobey my Lord, the chastisement of a great Day.\nمَنْ يُّصْرَفْ عَنْهُ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمَهٗؕ وَ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(16)\nMAN YYUSRAF A’NHO YAWMA-EZIN FAQAD RAHEMAH WA ZAA LEKA FAWZUL MOBEEN.\nFrom whomsoever it (the Chastisement) is averted on that day, indeed He had mercy on him; and this will be the manifest triumph ”.\nوَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهٗۤ اِلَّا هُوَؕ وَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ بِخَيْرٍ فَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(17)\nWA YYAMSASKA LAAHO BEZURRIN FALAA KAASHEFA LAHU ILLAA HOO WA YYAMSASKA BE-KHAYRIN FAHOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd if God toucheth thee with affliction, none can remove it but He; and if He toucheth thee with Good, then He hath power over all things.\nوَهُوَ الْقَاهِرُ فَوْقَ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(18)\nWA HOWA AL-QAAHERU FAWQA E’BAADEHI WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\nHe is the Supreme (Lord) above His servants; and He is the All-Wise and the All-Aware.\nقُلْ اَىُّ شَىْءٍ اَكْبَرُ شَهَادَةً ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ ۙ شَهِيْدٌ ۢ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْ وَاُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنُ لِاُنْذِرَكُمْ بِهٖ وَمَنْۢ بَلَغَ ؕ اَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُوْنَ اَنَّ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً اُخْرٰىؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَشْهَدُ ۚ قُلْ اِنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ وَّاِنَّنِىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَۘ‏(19)\nQUL AAA SHAY-IN AKBARO SHA-HAADATAN QOLIL LAAHO WA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WA OOHEYA ELAYYA HAAZAA QUR-AANO LEAUNZERAKUM BEHI WA MAN BALAGHA A-INNAKUM LATASHHADOONA ANNAL LAAHA LAAHE AALEHATAL AUKHRAA QUL LAA AASHHADU QUL INNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED WWAANNANEAA BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\nSay! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “What thing is the weightiest in testimony?” Say thou: “God is witness between me and you; and hath been revealed unto me this Qur’an that I may warn you with it, and whomsoever it reacheth; Do ye really bear witness that there are other gods with God?” Say thou: “I bear not (such) witness”! Say thou: Verily, Verily He is only one God and Verily I am away from that which ye associate (with Him).\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَعْرِفُوْنَهٗ كَمَا يَعْرِفُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَهُمُۘ اَ لَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(20)\nA’ZAABAN LLAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YA’REFOONAHU KAMAA YA’REFOONA AABNAAAHUMU A’ZAABAN LLAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThose whom We have given the Book recognise him (Muhammad), as they recognise their (own) sons; (yet) those who have lost their selves, they will not believe.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BEAAAYAATEH INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God or (he who) giveth the lie to His signs; verily the unjust will not succeed.\nوَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ نَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْۤا اَيْنَ شُرَكَآؤُكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA NAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ASHRAKOO AYNA SHURAKAAUKUMU LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nAnd on the day (of Judgment) We shall gather them all together, then We shall say to those who associated others “Where are your associate-gods whom ye used to conject?\nثُمَّ لَمْ تَكُنْ فِتْنَتُهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْا وَاللّٰهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(23)\nSUMMA LAM TAKUN FETNATUHUM ILLAA AN QAALOO WA LAAHE RABBENAA MAA KUNNAA MUSHREKEENA.\nThen their excuse would be nothing but that they would say: “By God, Our Lord! we were not polytheists.\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَذَبُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nAUNZUR KAYFA KAZABOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nBehold! how they lie against their own selves, and that which they forged has passed away from them.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُ اِلَيْكَ ۚ وَجَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا ؕ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كُلَّ اٰيَةٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهَا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءُوْكَ يُجَادِلُوْنَكَ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’U ELAYKA WA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AAKENNATAN AN YYAFQAHOOHU WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAN WA YYARAWA KULLA AAYATIM LAA YOAMENOO BEHAA HATTAA EZAA JAAOOKA YUJAADELOONAKA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nAnd of them are those who hearken unto thee, and We have cast veils over their hearts lest they understand it, and a heaviness into their ears; and together (even) if they see every sign they will not believe in it; to the extent that when they come to thee they only dispute with thee, those who disbelieve say: “This is naught but the legends of the ancients.\nوَهُمْ يَنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ وَيَنْئَوْنَ عَنْهُۚ وَاِنْ يُّهْلِكُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nWA HUM YANHAWNA A’NHO WAYANAWNA A’NHO WA YYUHLEKOONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThey prohibit (others) from it, and (themselves) keep far away from it; they only destroy their own selves, and (yet) they perceive (it) not.\nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ وُقِفُوْا عَلَى النَّارِ فَقَالُوْا يٰلَيْتَنَا نُرَدُّ وَلَا نُكَذِّبَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّنَا وَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ WUQEFOOA A’LAL NAAR FA-QAALOO YAALAYTANAA NURADDU WA LAA NUKAZZEBA BE-AAYAATIL RABBENAA WA NAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd couldst thou see when they are made confronting the (Hell) fire, then they shall say, “Would that we were sent back and we would not belie the signs of our Lord, and we would be of the believers.\nبَلْ بَدَا لَهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُخْفُوْنَ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَلَوْ رُدُّوْا لَعَادُوْا لِمَا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(28)\nBAL BADAA LAHUM MAA KAANOO YUKHFOONA MIN QABL WA WA LAW RUDDOOA LAA’AADOOA LEMAKH NUHOOA A’NHO WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nNay, it has been manifested to them what they did conceal before; and if they were sent back they would certainly return to what they were forbidden and most certainly they are liars.\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوْثِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QAALOO IN HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMABU’OOSEENA.\nAnd they say: “there is nothing (beyond’) this our life in this world, and we are not to be raised again.\nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ وُقِفُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ ؕ قَالَ اَلَيْسَ هٰذَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى وَرَبِّنَا ؕ قَالَ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ WUQEFOOA A’LAA RABBEHIM QAALA A-LAYSA HAAZAA BIL-HAQQE QAALOO BALAA WARABBENAA QAALA FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROONA.\nAnd couldst thou see when they are made to stand before their Lord, He will say: “Is this not the truth?” They will say: “Yes! by Our Lord!” He will say: “Taste ye then the chastisement for what ye did disbelieve.\nقَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ اللّٰهِؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً قَالُوْا يٰحَسْرَتَنَا عَلٰى مَا فَرَّطْنَا فِيْهَا ۙ وَهُمْ يَحْمِلُوْنَ اَوْزَارَهُمْ عَلٰى ظُهُوْرِهِمْؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَزِرُوْنَ‏(31)\nQAD KHASERA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE LAAH HATTAA EZAA JAAA-ATHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW QAALOO YAAHASRATANAA A’LAA MAA FARRATNAA FEEHAA WA HUM YAHMELOONA AAWZAARAHUM A’LAA ZUHOOREHEM ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAZEROONA.\nIndeed, are losers, they who disbelieved the meeting of God, until cometh suddenly upon them the hour (of Resurrection)’, They will say: “O’ Our grief for our neglecting it!” And they shall bear their burdens on their backs; Is it not evil indeed what they shall bear.\nوَ مَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاۤ اِلَّا لَعِبٌ وَّلَهْوٌ ؕ وَلَلدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(32)\nWA MAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA ILLAA LAE’EBUN WWALAHWUN WALALDDAARU AAKHERATO KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA YATTAQOONA AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd the life of this world is naught but play and vain sport; and certainly the abode of the hereafter, is the best for those who guard (themselves against evil); Do ye not then understand?\nقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اِنَّهٗ لَيَحْزُنُكَ الَّذِىْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَا يُكَذِّبُوْنَكَ وَلٰكِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(33)\nQAD NA’LAMO INNAHU LAYAHZUNUKA LAZEE YAQOOLOONA FA INNAHUM LAA YUKAZZEBOONAKA LAAKINNAL ZAALEMEEN BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nIndeed, We know, it certainly grieveth thee that which they say, but verily it is not thee (that) they belie, but (it is) the signs of God, the wrong doers deny.\nوَلَقَدْ كُذِّبَتْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَصَبَرُوْا عَلٰى مَا كُذِّبُوْا وَاُوْذُوْا حَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮهُمْ نَصْرُنَا ۚ وَلَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمٰتِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَكَ مِنْ نَّبَاِى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD KUZZEBAT RUSULUN MIN QABLEKA FA SABAROO A’LAA MAA KUZZEBOOA WAAWZOOA HATTAA ATAAHUM NASRUNAA WA LAA MUBADDELA LEKALEMAATE LAAHE WA LAQAD JAAA-AKA MIN NNABAAAA MURSALEEN.\nAnd most certainly were belied (Our) apostles before thee, but they were patient on their being belied and were persecuted until came to them Our help; and none can alter the words of God; And most certainly hath come to thee the tidings about the apostles (from Us).\nوَاِنْ كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيْكَ اِعْرَاضُهُمْ فَاِنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ اَنْ تَبْتَغِىَ نَفَقًا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَوْ سُلَّمًا فِى السَّمَآءِ فَتَاْتِيَهُمْ بِاٰيَةٍ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَمَعَهُمْ عَلَى الْهُدٰى فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(35)\nWA KAANA KABURA A’LAYKA AEA’RAAZUHUM FA-ENIN ASTATAA’TA AN TABTAGHEAAA NAFAQAN FIL ARZE AW SULLAMAN FIL SAMAAA-E FATAATEEHUM BE-AAYATIL WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAMAA’AHUM A’LAL HODAA FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nAnd if their turning away be hard upon thee, then if thou canst seek an opening (to go down) into the earth or a ladder (to ascend up) to heaven so that thou bringeth them a sign (a miracle) (it will be in vain) But if only God desireth, certainly would He have gathered them all on the (right) guidance, so be not thou of the ignorants.\nاِنَّمَا يَسْتَجِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْمَعُوْنَ ؕؔ وَالْمَوْتٰى يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُوْنَؔ‏(36)\nINNAMAA YASTAJEEBU LAZEENA YAS-MA-O’ONA WA MAWTAA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO SUMMA ELAYHE YURJAU’OONA.\nVerily, only those will accept thee, who listen (to the Word of God); and (as to) the dead, God will raise them, then unto Him will they return.\nوَ قَالُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يُّنَزِّلَ اٰيَةً وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA NUZZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH QUL INNAL LAAHA QAADERUN A’LAA AN YONAZZELAL AAYATAL WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd they say: “Why is not a sign sent down unto him from his Lord?” Say! “Verily God is able to send down a sign but most of them know not.\nوَمَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا طٰۤئِرٍ يَّطِيْرُ بِجَنَاحَيْهِ اِلَّاۤ اُمَمٌ اَمْثَالُكُمْؕ مَا فَرَّطْنَا فِى الْكِتٰبِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA MAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL FIL ARZE WA LAA TAAERIN YYATEERU BEJANAAHAYHE ILLAA OMAMUM AAMSAALUKUM MAA FARRATNAA FIL KETAABE MIN SHAY-IN SUMMA ELAA RABBEHIM YUHSHAROONA.\nThere is not an animal that walketh upon the earth, not a bird that flieth with its two wings, but they are communities the like of you; We have not neglected in the Book (The Qur’an), anything, then unto their Lord shall they (all) be gathered (in the end).\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا صُمٌّ وَّبُكْمٌ فِى الظُّلُمٰتِؕ مَنْ يَّشَاِ اللّٰهُ يُضْلِلْهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّشَاْ يَجْعَلْهُ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA SUMMUM WWABUKMUN FIL ZOLOMAAT MAN YYASHAA LAAHO YUZLELHU WA MAN YYASHAA YAJA’ALHU A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd they who belied Our signs are deaf and dumb, in utter darkness; whom God pleaseth He alloweth them to go astray; and whom He pleaseth, He doth put them on the straight path.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتَكُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُ اللّٰهِ اَوْ اَ تَتْكُمُ السَّاعَةُ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَدْعُوْنَۚ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(40)\nQUL AARAAYTAKUM IN AATAAKUM A’ZAABO LAAHE AW A’ZAABAN TATKUMU SAA-A’TO AAGHAYRA LAAHE TADU’OONA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Think ye that if cometh to you the chastisement of God, or cometh to you the Hour (of resurrection), will ye call (for help) other than God, (say ye it out) if ye are truthful.\nبَلْ اِيَّاهُ تَدْعُوْنَ فَيَكْشِفُ مَا تَدْعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ اِنْ شَآءَ وَتَنْسَوْنَ مَا تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(41)\nBAL IYYAAHO TADU’OONA FAYAKSHEFU MAA TADU’OONA ELAYHE IN SHAAA-AL WA TANSAWNA MAA TUSHREKOONA.\nNay, Him will ye call upon, and He cleareth away which ye pray for unto Him if He pleaseth, and ye would forget (the false gods’) ye set up (with Him).\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْبَاْسَآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَضَرَّعُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA OMAMIN MIN QABLEKA FAAKHAZNAAHUM BE-BAA-SAAA-E WAZ ZARRAAA-E LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZARRAU’OONA.\nAnd most certainly We sent (apostles) unto peoples before thee, then We caught them in distress and adversity, in order they might humble themselves.\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا تَضَرَّعُوْا وَلٰكِنْ قَسَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nFA-LAWLAA IZ JAAA-AHUM BAASUNAA TAZARRAU’OOA WA LAAKIL QASAT QULOOBUHUM WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUL SHAYTAANO MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nYet why did they not, when our punishment came to them, humble themselves? but their hearts were hardened and the devil made fair-seeming for them, what they did act.\nفَلَمَّا نَسُوْا مَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖ فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَبْوَابَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا فَرِحُوْا بِمَاۤ اُوْتُوْۤا اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بَغْتَةً فَاِذَا هُمْ مُّبْلِسُوْنَ‏(44)\nFALAMMAA NASOOA MAA ZUKKEROOA BEHI FATAHNA A’LAYHIM AABWAABA KULLE SHAY-IN HATTAA EZAA FAREHOO BEMAA OOTOO AAKHAZNAAHUM BAGHTATANW FA-EZAA HUM MMUBLESOONA.\nAnd when they forgot that which they had been admonished, We opened for them the doors of all things (of enjoyments); until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We caught them suddenly, when lo! they were in utter despair.\nفَقُطِعَ دَابِرُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ؕ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(45)\nFAQUTEA’A DAABERU QAWMIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO WA HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nSo, the roots of the people who were unjust were cut off; and all praise is God’s the Lord of the worlds.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ سَمْعَكُمْ وَ اَبْصَارَكُمْ وَخَتَمَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِكُمْ مَّنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِهؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ ثُمَّ هُمْ يَصْدِفُوْنَ‏(46)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN AAKHAZA LAAHO SAMA’AKUM WA AABSAARAKUM WA KHATAMAL A’LAA QOLOOBEKUM MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRO LAAHE YAATEEKUM BEH AUNZUR KAYFA NUSARREFU AAYAATE SUMMA HUM YASDEFOONA.\nSay: “Think ye, that if God taketh away your hearing and your sight and sealeth on your hearts, who is the god other than God that can bring it (again) to you?” See thou, how We display (explaining) the signs yet they turn aside.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتَكُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُ اللّٰهِ بَغْتَةً اَوْ جَهْرَةً هَلْ يُهْلَكُ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(47)\nQUL AARAAYTAKUM IN AATAAKUM A’ZAABO LAAHE BAGHTATANW AW JAHRATN HAL YUHLAKU ILLAA AL-QAWMU ZAALEMOON.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) “Think ye, if the chastisement of God cometh to you suddenly or openly, will any be destroyed but the unjust people?\nوَمَا نُرْسِلُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَۚ فَمَنْ اٰمَنَ وَاَصْلَحَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA MAA NURSELU MURSALEEN ILLAA MOBASH-SHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN FAMAN AAMANA WAASLAHA FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nAnd We send not messengers but (as) heralds with glad tidings and warners; then whoever believeth and acteth aright, they shall have no fear, nor shall they grieve.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَمَسُّهُمُ الْعَذَابُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(49)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA YAMASSUHUMU A’ZAABO BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nAnd (as for) those who belie our signs, chastisement shall afflict them for what they used to transgress.\nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ خَزَآئِنُ اللّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ وَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ اِنِّىْ مَلَكٌ ۚ اِنْ اَتَّبِعُ اِلَّا مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ ؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(50)\nQUL LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM E’ENDEAA KHAZAAENUS LAAHE WA LAA A-A’LAMO GHAYBA WA LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM INNEE MALAKUN IN AATTABEU’U ILLAA MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA QUL HAL YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU AFALAA TATAFAKKAROONA.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I do not say unto you (that) with me are the treasures of God, nor do I know the unseen, nor do I say unto you that I am an angel; I follow not but what is revealed unto me;” Say, “Are the blind and the seeing alike; Do ye not then reflect?\nوَاَنْذِرْ بِهِ الَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ اَنْ يُّحْشَرُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ وَلِىٌّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٌ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(51)\nWAANZER BEHIL LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA AN YYUHSHAROOA ELAA RABBEHIM LAYSA LAHUM MIN DOONEHI WALIYYUN WA LAA SHAFEEA’UN LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nAnd warn thou with it, the Qur’an those who fear that they shall be gathered unto their Lord (Thinking that) there shall not be for them, besides Him, any guardian or an intercessor, happily they may guard (themselves against evil).\nوَلَا تَطْرُدِ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَدٰوةِ وَالْعَشِىِّ يُرِيْدُوْنَ وَجْهَهٗ ؕ مَا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ حِسَابِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ وَّمَا مِنْ حِسَابِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَتَطْرُدَهُمْ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(52)\nWA LAA TATRUDE LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA RABBAHUM BIL-GHADAAWTE WAL A’ASHEAAAE YOREEDOONA WAJHAHU MAA A’LAYKA MIN HESAABEHEM MIN SHAY-IN WA MAA MIN HESAABEKA A’LAYHIM MIN SHAY-IN FATATRUDAHUM FA TAKOONA MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd drive not away those who call upon their Lord, in the morning and the evening, they seek His countenance; neither it is on thee to answer for anything on their account nor is it on them to answer for anything on thine account so that thou driveth them away and thus be of the unjust.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ فَتَنَّا بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لِّيَقُوْلُوْۤا اَهٰٓؤُلَآءِ مَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِنَا ؕ اَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَمَ بِالشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA KAZAALEKA FATANNAL BA’ZAHUM BE-BA’Z LLEEQOOLOOA AAHAAAULAAE MANNA LAAHO A’LAYHIM MIN BAYNENAA A-LAYSA LAAHO BE-A’ALAMA BEALSSHAAKEREENA.\nThus, did We try some of them by others so that they say: “Are these they upon whom God hath conferred (His) favours, from among us? Doth not God know best the grateful?\nوَاِذَا جَآءَكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَقُلْ سَلَمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلٰى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ ۙ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ عَمِلَ مِنْكُمْ سُوْٓءًۢا بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ تَابَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ وَاَصْلَحَۙ فَاَنَّهٗ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(54)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AKA LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATENAA FAQUL SALAMUN A’LAYKUM KATABAL RABBOKUM A’LAA NAFSEHE AR-RAHMATA ANNAHU MAN A’MELA MINKUM SOOO-AN BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA TAABA MIN BA’DEHI WAASLAHA FA ANNAHU GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd when come unto thee, those who believe in Our signs, say: “Salamun-alaikum” (Peace be on you) your Lord hath prescribed mercy on Himself, (so that) if anyone of you doth evil in ignorance, then turneth (repentant) after that and amendeth (himself), then verily He is the Most-Forgiving, The Most-Merciful.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلِتَسْتَبِيْنَ سَبِيْلُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(55)\nWA KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE WALETASTABEENA SABEELU MUJREMEEN.\nAnd thus We explain the signs in details so that the way of the sinners may be manifest.\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ نُهِيْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَ تَّبِعُ اَهْوَآءَكُمْۙ قَدْ ضَلَلْتُ اِذًا وَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(56)\nQUL INNEE NUHEETU AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAH QUL LAA A’ZAABAN TTABEU’U AAHWAAAKUM QAD ZALALTU EZAL WA MAA ANAA MENAL AL-MUHTADEENA.\nSay! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I am forbidden to worship those whom ye call besides God;” Say Thou: “I follow not your inclinations for then indeed I should have gone astray and I will not be of those who are guided (aright).\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَكَذَّبْتُمْ بِهٖؕ مَا عِنْدِىْ مَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِهٖؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ يَقُصُّ الْحَقَّ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْفٰصِلِيْنَ‏(57)\nQUL INNEE A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WA KAZZABTUM BEH MAA E’ENDEAA MAA TAS-TA’JELOONA BEH ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH YAQUSSO HAQQA WA HOWA KHAYRUR AL-FAASELEENA.\nSay thou: “Verily I have manifest proof from my Lord and you belied it; I have not with me that (chastisement) which ye hasten for; the judgment belongeth (to none) but unto God; Who declareth the truth and He is the best decider.\nقُلْ لَّوْ اَنَّ عِنْدِىْ مَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِهٖ لَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(58)\nQUL LAW ANNAL E’ENDEAA MAA TAS-TA’JELOONA BEHI LAQOZEYA MIN BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nSay thou, “If it were with me, what ye hasten for, certainly would have been decided the matter between me and you; and God knoweth best the unjust.\nوَعِنْدَهٗ مَفَاتِحُ الْغَيْبِ لَا يَعْلَمُهَاۤ اِلَّا هُوَؕ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ وَمَا تَسْقُطُ مِنْ وَّرَقَةٍ اِلَّا يَعْلَمُهَا وَلَا حَبَّةٍ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْاَرْضِ وَلَا رَطْبٍ وَّلَا يَابِسٍ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(59)\nWA I’NDAHU MAFAATEHUL GHAYBE LAA YA’LAMOHAA ILLAA HOO, WA YA’LAMO MAA FIL BARRE WAL BAHR, WA MAA TASQOTO MINW WARAQATIN ILLAA YA’LAMOHAA WA LAA HABBATIN FEE ZOLOMAATIL ARZE WA LAA RATBINW WA LAA YAABESIN ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nAnd with Him are the keys (of the treasures) of the unseen - knoweth it not anyone but He; and He (alone) knoweth what is in the land and the sea; and (there) falleth not (even) a leaf (of a tree) but He knoweth it, nor a grain in the darkness (in the deepest parts) of the earth, nor anything wet or dry but (it is) in a clear Book.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ بِالَّيْلِ وَ يَعْلَمُ مَا جَرَحْتُمْ بِالنَّهَارِ ثُمَّ يَبْعَثُكُمْ فِيْهِ لِيُقْضٰٓى اَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّىۚ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YATAWAFFAAKUM BIL-LAYLE WA YA’LAMO MAA JARAHTUM BEALNNAHAARE SUMMA YABA’ASUKUM FEEHE LEEQZAAA AJALUM AJALIM SUMMA ELAYHE MARJE-O’KUM SUMMA YUNABBEUKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd He it is who taketh you away at night (in sleep), and He knoweth what ye acquire in the day, then He raiseth you up therein that a pre-fixed term (of life) be fulfilled; then unto Him is your (ultimate) return, then He will declare unto you what ye were doing.\nوَهُوَ الْقَاهِرُ فَوْقَ عِبَادِهٖ وَيُرْسِلُ عَلَيْكُمْ حَفَظَةً ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَ اَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ تَوَفَّتْهُ رُسُلُنَا وَهُمْ لَا يُفَرِّطُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA HOWA AL-QAAHERU FAWQA E’BAADEHI WA YURSELUR A’LAYKUM HAFAZATAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AHADAKOMUL MAWTO TAWAFFATHU ROSOLONAA WA HUM LAA YUFARRETOONA.\nAnd He is the All-dominant above His subservient ones, and He sendeth over you the guard; until cometh death unto one of you, Our messengers (angels) take him away, and they are not remiss.\nثُمَّ رُدُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَوْلٰٮهُمُ الْحَقِّؕ اَلَا لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَهُوَ اَسْرَعُ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ‏(62)\nSUMMA RUDDOOA ELAL LAAHE MAWLAAHUMU HAQQ ALAA LAHUL HUKMO WA HOWA AASRAU’U AL-HAASEBEENA.\nThen they are returned unto God, their Maula (Master), the (only) Real One; Beware! (Now surely), His (alone) (as the Master) is the Judgment, and He is the Swiftest of reckoners.\nقُلْ مَنْ يُّنَجِّيْكُمْ مِّنْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ تَدْعُوْنَهٗ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخُفْيَةًۚ لَئِنْ اَنْجٰٮنَا مِنْ هٰذِهٖ لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(63)\nQUL MAN YYUNAJJEEKUM MIN ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE TADU’OONAH TAZARRUA’AN WWAKHUFYATAN LAIL AANJAANAA MIN HAAZEHI LANAKOONANNA MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nSay thou: “Who delivereth you from the (dread of the) darkness of the land and the sea, (when) ye pray to Him (openly) humiliating yourselves, and secretly (saying)”; “If He delivereth us from this, certainly we shall he of the grateful ones.\nقُلِ اللّٰهُ يُنَجِّيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا وَمِنْ كُلِّ كَرْبٍ ثُمَّ اَنْتُمْ تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(64)\nQOLIL LAAHO YUNAJJEEKUM MINHAA WA MIN KULLE KARBIN SUMMA ANTUM TUSHREKOONA.\nSay Thou: “God delivereth you from them, and from every distress, yet again ye associate (others) with Him.\nقُلْ هُوَ الْقَادِرُ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّبْعَثَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابًا مِّنْ فَوْقِكُمْ اَوْ مِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِكُمْ اَوْ يَلْبِسَكُمْ شِيَعًا وَّيُذِيْقَ بَعْضَكُمْ بَاْسَ بَعْضٍؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(65)\nQUL HOWA AL-QAADERU A’LAA AN YYABA’ASA A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAN MIN FAWQEKUM AW MIN TAHTE AARJULEKUM AW YALBESAKUM AHLAHAA WWAYUZEEQA BAA’ZAKUM BAASA BA’Z WA AUNZUR KAYFA NUSARREFU AAYAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YAFQAHOON.\nSay thou: “He hath power that He may send on you a chastisement from above you or from under your feet or He should involve you in confusion (in) party (dissensions) and make some of you taste the fighting of others;” Behold! how repeatedly do We display the signs, that they may understand.\nوَكَذَّبَ بِهٖ قَوْمُكَ وَهُوَ الْحَقُّ ؕ قُلْ لَّسْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِوَكِيْلٍؕ‏(66)\nWA KAZZABA BEHI QAWMUKA WA HOWA HAQQO QUL LLASTU A’LAYKUM BEWAKEELIN.\nAnd belied it thy people and it is the very truth. Say: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I am not a guard upon you.\nلِّكُلِّ نَبَاٍ مُّسْتَقَرٌّ وَّسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(67)\nLEKULLE NABAA MMUSTAQARRUN WWASAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nFor every prophecy is (prefixed) time, And soon shall ye know it.\nوَاِذَا رَاَيْتَ الَّذِيْنَ يَخُوْضُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى يَخُوْضُوْا فِىْ حَدِيْثٍ غَيْرِهٖ ؕ وَاِمَّا يُنْسِيَنَّكَ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَلَا تَقْعُدْ بَعْدَ الذِّكْرٰى مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(68)\nWA EZAA RA-AYTA LAZEENA YAKHOOZOONA FEE AAYAATENAA FAAA’REZ A’NHUM HATTAA YAKHOOZOOA FEE HADEESIN GHAYREH WA AMMAA YUNSEENNAKA SHAYTAANO FALAA TAQU’UD BA’DA ZIKRAA LAAHA QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when thou seest those cavilling about Our signs, get thee away from them until they enter into (some) other discourse; And if the devil causeth thee to forget (this), then sit not after recollection, with the unjust people.\nوَمَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ مِنْ حِسَابِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ وَّلٰكِنْ ذِكْرٰى لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA MAA A’LAL LAZEENA YATTAQOON MIN HESAABEHEM MIN SHAY-IN LAAKIL ZEKRAA LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nAnd nothing of the reckoning of their (deed) shall be upon those who guard (themselves against evil), but only to remind, so that they may guard (themselves against evil).\nوَذَرِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لَعِبًا وَّلَهْوًا وَّغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَ ذَكِّرْ بِهٖۤ اَنْ تُبْسَلَ نَفْسٌ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْۖ لَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِىٌّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٌ ۚ وَاِنْ تَعْدِلْ كُلَّ عَدْلٍ لَّا يُؤْخَذْ مِنْهَا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اُبْسِلُوْا بِمَا كَسَبُوْا ۚ لَهُمْ شَرَابٌ مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّعَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nWAZARE LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA DEENAHUM LAE’EBAN WWALAHWAN WWAGHARRATHUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA WA ZAKKER BEHI AN TUBSALA NAFSUN BEMAA KASABAT LAYSA LAHAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYUN WA LAA SHAFEEA’UN WA TAA’DEL KULLA ZAWAY LAA YUKHAZ MINHAA OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AUBSELOOA BEMAA KASABOO LAHUM SHARAABUN MIN HAMEEMIN WWAA’AZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nAnd leave those who have taken their religion for a play and a vain sport, and (whom) the (temporal) Life of this world hath beguiled, and admonish (them) thou by it (the Qur’an) lest a soul be fettered with what it hath earned, for it, shall not be besides God any protector nor an intercessor and if it seeketh to give every compensation, it shall not be accepted from it; these are those fettered with what they did earn, for them shall be a drink of boiling water and a painful chastisement for what they used to disbelieve.\nقُلْ اَنَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُنَا وَلَا يَضُرُّنَا وَنُرَدُّ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِنَا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ كَالَّذِى اسْتَهْوَتْهُ الشَّيٰطِيْنُ فِى الْاَرْضِ حَيْرَانَ لَهٗۤ اَصْحٰبٌ يَّدْعُوْنَهٗۤ اِلَى الْهُدَى ائْتِنَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ هُدَى اللّٰهِ هُوَ الْهُدٰىؕ وَاُمِرْنَا لِنُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(71)\nQUL AANADU’OOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UNAA WA LAA YAZURRUNAA WANURADDU A’LAA AAA’QAABENAA BA’DA IZ HADAANAA LAAHO KA-LAZIS ASTAHWATHU SHAYAATEENO FIL ARZE HAYRAANA LAHU AASHAABUN YYADU’OONAH ELAL AL-HUDAA E-ATENAA QUL INNAL HODAL LAAHE HOWA HODAA WA WAAMERNAA LENUSLEMA LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay (Ask O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!); “Shall we call on (any) besides God which profiteth us not nor harmeth us, and shall we turn back on our heels after God hath guided us, like him who is infatuated by the devils, in the earth perplexed? (though’) he hath companions who call unto guidance saying: “Come unto us;” Say: “Verily the guidance of God, that is the (true) guidance; and we are commanded that we should submit (ourselves) unto the Lord of the worlds,\nوَاَنْ اَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اتَّقُوْهُ ؕ وَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(72)\nWA AAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA ATTAQOOHU WA HOWA LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nAnd that ye establish prayer, and ye fear Him; And He it is unto Whom ye shall be gathered.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَيَوْمَ يَقُوْلُ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُؕ قَوْلُهُ الْحَقُّ ؕ وَلَهُ الْمُلْكُ يَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ ؕ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَ الشَّهَادَةِ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(73)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ WA YAWMA YAQOOLO KUN FAYAKOONU QAWLUHU HAQQO LAHUL A’LAYNAA YAWMA YUNFAKHO FIL SOORE A’ALEMUL GHAYBE WA ASH-SHAHAADATE WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\nAnd He it is Who created the heavens and the earth with Truth; and the day He sayeth “Be,” it “Is.” His word is the truth; His is the kingdom on the day when (Spirits) will be breathed into forms (Trumpet); the Knower of the unseen and the evident (worlds); And He is the All-Wise and the All- Aware.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ لِاَبِيْهِ اٰزَرَ اَتَتَّخِذُ اَصْنَامًا اٰلِهَةً  ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكَ وَقَوْمَكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(74)\nWA IZ QAALA AEBRAAHEEMU LEAABEEHE AAAZARA AATATTAKHEZU AASNAAMAN AALEHATAL INNEE AARAAKA WAQAWMAKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nAnd when said Abraham unto his father, Azar, “Dost thou take idols for gods? Verily I see thee and thy people in obvious error!\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُرِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ مَلَكُوْتَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلِيَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُوْقِنِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA KAZAALEKA NUREAA IBRAAHEEMA MALAKOOTA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LEYAKOONA MENAL AL-MOOQENEENA.\nAnd, thus did We show Abraham (the governing of) the Kingdom of the heavens and the earth and that he may be of those who are sure.\nفَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيْهِ الَّيْلُ رَاٰ كَوْكَبًا ۚ قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَ قَالَ لَاۤ اُحِبُّ الْاٰفِلِيْنَ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA JANNA A’LAYHE LAYL RAA KAWKABAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE FALAMMAA AAFALA QAALA LAA AUHEBBU AL-AAAFELEENA.\n(Thereafter) when the night overshadowed him, saw he a star; said he; “This my Lord?” And then when it did set, said he: “Hove not the setting ones.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَالْقَمَرَ بَازِغًا قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَ قَالَ لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَهْدِنِىْ رَبِّىْ لَاَ كُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الضَّآ لِّيْنَ‏(77)\nFALAMMAA RAAALQAMARA BAAZEGHAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE FALAMMAA AAFALA QAALA LAIL LAM YAHDENEAA RABBEE LAA KOONANNA MENAL QAWMIL LAMENAZ ZAAAL-LEEN.\nThen when he saw the moon rising (in splendour), said he: “This my Lord?” And when it did set, said he: “Had not my Lord guided me, I would have certainly been of the erring people.\nفَلَمَّا رَاٰ الشَّمْسَ بَازِغَةً قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ هٰذَاۤ اَكْبَرُۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَتْ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(78)\nFALAMMAA RAA SHAMSA BAAZEGHATAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE HAAZAA AKBARO FALAMMAA AAFALAT QAALA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\nThen when he saw the sun rising (in splendour), said he: “This my Lord?” This is the greatest (one), “And then when it (also) did set, said he; “O’ my people! I am clear of what ye associate with God.\nاِنِّىْ وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِىَ لِلَّذِىْ فَطَرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ حَنِيْفًا وَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَۚ‏(79)\nINNEE WAJJAHTU WAJHEAAA LIL-LAZEE FATARA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA HANEEFAA WA MAA ANAA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nVerily I have turned my face (myself) wholly unto Him Who originated the heavens and the earth, being upright, and I am not of the associators.\nوَحَآجَّهٗ قَوْمُهٗ ؕ قَالَ اَتُحَآجُّٓونِّىْ فِى اللّٰهِ وَقَدْ هَدٰٮنِؕ وَلَاۤ اَخَافُ مَا تُشْرِكُوْنَ بِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ رَبِّىْ شَيْئًا ؕ وَسِعَ رَبِّىْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًاؕ اَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWAHAAJJAH QAWMOHU QAALA AATUHAAJJOOONNEAA FIL LAAHE WA QAD HADAANE WA LAA AKHAAFO MAA TUSHREKOONA BEHI ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL RABBEE SHAY-ANW WASEA’ RABBEE KULLA SHAY-IN E’ELMAN AFALAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nAnd (when) disputed with him, his people; Said he: “Do ye dispute with me about God? while indeed He hath guided me; I fear not (anything) of what ye associate with Him, save that (which) My Lord willeth; My Lord comprehendeth everything in His knowledge; Will ye not then mind?\nوَكَيْفَ اَخَافُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكْتُمْ وَلَا تَخَافُوْنَ اَنَّكُمْ اَشْرَكْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطٰنًا ؕ فَاَىُّ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ اَحَقُّ بِالْاَمْنِۚ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَۘ‏(81)\nWA KAYFA AKHAAFO MAA AASHRAKTUM WA LAA TAKHAAFOONA ANNAKUM AASHRAKTUM BIL-LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI A’LAYKUM SULTAANAN FAAAAAU AL-FAREEQAYNE AHAQQO BIL-AAMNE IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd how should I fear of what ye have associated with Him, while ye fear not that ye have associated with God that for which hath not been sent down any authority; Which then of the two parties hath greater right to security, if ye (only) know?\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَمْ يَلْبِسُوْۤا اِيْمَانَهُمْ بِظُلْمٍ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ الْاَمْنُ وَهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(82)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA LAM YALBESOOA AEEMAANAHUM BEZULMIN AOOLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-AAMNU WA HUM HUM MOHTADOON.\nThose who believe and mix not their faith with iniquity, those are they for whom is security, and they are (the ones) guided aright.\nوَتِلْكَ حُجَّتُنَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖؕ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجٰتٍ مَّنْ نَّشَآءُ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(83)\nWA TILKAL HUJJATUNAA AAATAYNAAHAA IBRAAHEEMA A’LAA QAWMEH NARFAU’U DARAJAATIN MAN NNASHAAU INNAL RABBAKA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nThis Our argument, We gave it to Abraham against his people; We exalt (any one) whom We please; Verily thy Lord is All Wise, All-Knowing.\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَؕ كُلًّا هَدَيْنَا ۚ وَنُوْحًا هَدَيْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ دَاوٗدَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ وَاَيُّوْبَ وَيُوْسُفَ وَمُوْسٰى وَ هٰرُوْنَؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(84)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WAYAA’QOOBA KULLAN HADAYNAA WA ARSALNAA HADAYNAA MIN QABLO WA MIN ZURREETEH DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA WAAYYOOBA WAYOOSUFA WA MOOSAA WA HAAROONA WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nWe gave unto him (Abraham) (issues like) Isaac and Jacob; each We did guide, and Noah, We did guided before, and in his progeny, David and Solomon, and Job and Joseph and Moses and Aaron; and thus do We reward those who do good.\nوَزَكَرِيَّا وَيَحْيٰى وَعِيْسٰى وَاِلْيَاسَؕ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَۙ‏(85)\nWAZAKAREEA WAYAHYAA WA E’ESAA WAALYAASA KULLUL MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd Zakariya and John and Jesus and Elias; everyone was of the righteous (ones).\nوَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَالْيَسَعَ وَيُوْنُسَ وَلُوْطًا ؕ وَكُلًّا فَضَّلْنَا عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(86)\nWA ISMAA-E’ELA WAL YASAA’A WAYOONUSA WA LOOTAN WAKULLAN FAZZALNAA A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd Ishmael and Elisha and Jonah and Lot; and everyone We did exalt (with Our apostle-ship) over the worlds.\nوَمِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ وَاِخْوَانِهِمْۚ وَاجْتَبَيْنٰهُمْ وَهَدَيْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(87)\nWA MIN AAABAAEHEM WAZURREETEHEM WAAKHWAANEHEM WAAJTABAYNAAHUM WAHADAYNAAHUM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd of their fathers and their descendants and their brethren, and We did choose them (for Our apostleship), and We guided them unto the straight (right) way.\nذٰ لِكَ هُدَى اللّٰهِ يَهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖؕ وَلَوْ اَشْرَكُوْا لَحَبِطَ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(88)\nZAA LEKA HODAL LAAHE YAHDEE BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’EBAADEH WA LAW ASHRAKOO LAHABETA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThis is God’s guidance guideth He with it, whomsoever of His servants He pleaseth; and if they were to associate others (with Him ) certainly would be vain for them what they were doing.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ ؕ فَاِنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهَا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ فَقَدْ وَكَّلْنَا بِهَا قَوْمًا لَّيْسُوْا بِهَا بِكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(89)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA WAL HUKMA WA NOBUWWATA FA-IN YAKFUR BEHAA HAAOOLAAA-E FAQAD WAKKALNAA BEHAA QAWMAN LLAYSOOA BEHAA BE-KAAFEREEN.\nThese are they whom gave We the Book and the authority and the apostleship; so if these (people) disbelieve in it, indeed have We (already) entrusted it unto a people who are not disbelievers in it.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ هَدَى اللّٰهُ فَبِهُدٰٮهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ ؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا ؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(90)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LAZEENA LAAHO FABEHUDAAHUMU AQTADEH QUL LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN IN HOWA ILLAA ZEKRAA LIL-A’AALAMEENA.\nThese are they whom God hath guideth, therefore follow their guidance; Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!)’. “I ask not any recompense from you on it (the apostleship); it is naught but a reminder to the worlds.\nوَمَا قَدَرُوا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖۤ اِذْ قَالُوْا مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى بَشَرٍ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ قُلْ مَنْ اَنْزَلَ الْكِتٰبَ الَّذِىْ جَآءَ بِهٖ مُوْسٰى نُوْرًا وَّ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ تَجْعَلُوْنَهٗ قَرَاطِيْسَ تُبْدُوْنَهَا وَتُخْفُوْنَ كَثِيْرًا ۚ وَعُلِّمْتُمْ مَّا لَمْ تَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنْتُمْ وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُكُمْؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُۙ ثُمَّ ذَرْهُمْ فِىْ خَوْضِهِمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَ‏(91)\nWA MAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH IZ QAALOO MAA ANZALAL LAAHO A’LAA BASHARIN MIN SHAY-IN QUL MAN ANZALAL KETAABA LAZEE JAAA-A BEHI MOOSAA NOORAN WA HODAM LIN-NAASE TAJA’ALOONAH QARAATEESA TUBDOONAHAA WA TUKHFOONA KASEERAA WAU’ULLEMTUM MAA LAM TA’LAMOO ANTUM WA LAA AAABAAUKUM QOLIL LAAHO SUMMA ZARHUM FEE KHAWZEHEM YALA’ABOONA.\nThey esteem not God with the estimation due to Him when they say: “Nothing did God send down unto man!” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Who (then) did it send down the Book which Moses brought? a light and a guidance to mankind, ye make (transcribe) it into papers (whereof) ye publish (a part) and conceal ye much (of it)? and ye were taught what ye knew not, neither you nor your fathers; Say thou! “God!” then leave them sporting in their vain discourses.\nوَهٰذَا كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مُبٰرَكٌ مُّصَدِّقُ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَلِتُنْذِرَ اُمَّ الْقُرٰى وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ وَهُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَ‏(92)\nWA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO MUBAARAKUN MMUSADDEQU LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WA LETUNZERA AUMMA KORAA WA MAN HAWLAHAA WAL LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE YOAMENOONA BEHI WA HUM A’LAA SALAATEHIM YUHAAFEZOONA.\nThis Book, (The Qur’an) We have sent it down blessed, confirming that which hath been before it, and that thou mayest warn (the people of) the Mother City (Mecca) and those around her; and those who believe in the Hereafter believe in it, and they on their prayers are constantly guarding.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ قَالَ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ وَلَمْ يُوْحَ اِلَيْهِ شَىْءٌ وَّمَنْ قَالَ سَاُنْزِلُ مِثْلَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُؕ وَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ فِىْ غَمَرٰتِ الْمَوْتِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ بَاسِطُوْۤا اَيْدِيْهِمْۚ اَخْرِجُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمُؕ اَلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ الْهُوْنِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَكُنْتُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِهٖ تَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW QAALA OOHEYA ELAYYA WA LAM YOOHA ELAYHE SHAY-UN WWAMAN QAALA SAANZELU MISLA MAA ANZALAL LAAH WA LAW TARAAA EZIM ZAALEMOON FEE GHAMARAATE MAWT WAL MALAAA-EKATO BAASETOOA AYDEEHIM AKHREJOO AANFUSAKUMU AL-YAWMA TUJZAWNA A’ZAABAL HOONE BEMAA KUNTUM TAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE GHAYRA HAQQE WA KUNTUM A’N AAYAATEHI TASTAKBEROONA.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God, or sayeth “It hath been revealed unto me” while nothing had been revealed unto him, and he who sayeth: “I can jet down the like of what God rath sent down;” and if thou hadst seen when the unjust shall re in the agonies of death and the angels shall spread forth their hands, saying: “Surrender ye your souls; today ye shall be recompensed with a disgracing chastisement for what ye spoke against God other than the truth and (because) ye used to behave with pride against His signs.\nوَلَقَدْ جِئْتُمُوْنَا فُرَادٰى كَمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّتَرَكْتُمْ مَّا خَوَّلْنٰكُمْ وَرَآءَ ظُهُوْرِكُمْۚ وَمَا نَرٰى مَعَكُمْ شُفَعَآءَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ اَنَّهُمْ فِيْكُمْ شُرَكٰٓؤُا ؕ لَقَدْ تَّقَطَّعَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْكُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(94)\nWA LAQAD JETUMOONAA FURAADAA KAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM AWWALA MARRAH WWATARAKTUM MAA KHAWLNAAKUM WARAAA-A ZUHOOREKUM WA MAA NARAA MA-A’KUM SHUFAA’AAAKUMU LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM ANNAHUM FEEKUM SHURAKAAAUA LAQAD TTAQATTAA’A BAYNAKUM WA ZALLA A’NKUM MAA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nAnd indeed ye come to us (bare and) alone as We created you at first, and ye have left behind your backs what We bestowed on you, and We see not with you your intercessors, those whom ye asserted that they were, in your affairs the associates (of God); and indeed are now severed the ties between you, and hath gone away from you what ye (falsely) asserted.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ فَالِقُ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰىؕ يُخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَمُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتِ مِنَ الْحَىِّ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ فَاَنّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(95)\nINNAL LAAHA FAALEQU AL-HABBE WAALNNAWAA KHAB-A HAYYA MENAL MAYYETE WA WAMUKHREJU MAYYETE WA MENAL HAYYE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\nVerily God is the Splitter of (seed) grain and the (date) stone (to sprout); He bringeth out the living from the dead and He is the Bringer of the dead from the living; That is God! How then are ye turned (deluded) away.\nفَالِقُ الْاِصْبَاحِۚ وَ جَعَلَ الَّيْلَ سَكَنًا وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ حُسْبَانًا ؕ ذٰلِكَ تَقْدِيْرُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِ‏(96)\nFAALEQU AL-AESBAAHE WA JA-A’LA LAYLA SAKANAN WWAALSSHAMSA WAL QAMARA HUSBAANAN ZAALEKA TAQDEERUL A’ZEEZIL AL-A’ALEEME.\nHe the Cleaver of the dawn; and hath made the night for rest, and the sun and the moon for reckoning (time); This is the measuring of the Almighty, the All-Knowing (Lord).\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ النُّجُوْمَ لِتَهْتَدُوْا بِهَا فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(97)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL AN-NUJOOMA LE-NASAARAA BEHAA FEE ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nAnd He it is who made the stars for you that ye may be (rightly) guided by (observing) them in the darkness of the land and the sea. Indeed, have We made plain the signs for the people who (can) know.\nوَ هُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ فَمُسْتَقَرٌّ وَّمُسْتَوْدَعٌ ؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّفْقَهُوْنَ‏(98)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AN-SHA-A MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN FA MUSTAQARRUNW WWAMUSTAWDAA’UN QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YYAFQAHOONA.\nHe it is who hath produced you from one soul, then there is (for you) a receptacle and a depository; we have made plain the signs for a people who understand.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً ۚ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖ نَبَاتَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ فَاَخْرَجْنَا مِنْهُ خَضِرًا نُّخْرِجُ مِنْهُ حَبًّا مُّتَرَاكِبًا ۚ وَمِنَ النَّخْلِ مِنْ طَلْعِهَا قِنْوَانٌ دَانِيَةٌ وَّجَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ اَعْنَابٍ وَّالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالرُّمَّانَ مُشْتَبِهًا وَّغَيْرَ مُتَشَابِهٍ ؕ اُنْظُرُوْۤا اِلٰى ثَمَرِهٖۤ اِذَاۤ اَثْمَرَ وَيَنْعِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI NABAATA KULLE SHAY-IN FA AKH-RAJNAA MINHO KHAZERAN NNUKHREJU MINHO HABBANW MMUTARAAKEBAN WA MENAN AN-NAKHLE MIN TALE’EHAA QENWAANUN DAANEETUN WA MIN AAA’NAABIN WWAALZZAYTOONA WAALRRUMMAANA MUSHTABEHAN WWAGHAYRA MUTASHAABEHIN AUNZUROOA ELAA SAMAREHI EZAA AASMARA WAYANE’EH INNAL FEE ZAA ZAALEKUM LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nHe it is who sendeth down water from heaven, then We bring forth with it buds of (all plants) from it green (foliage) from which We produced grain piled up in the ears; and of the palm-tree, of the sheaths of it, come forth clusters (of dates) within reach, and gardens of grapes and Olives and pomegranates, alike and unlike; see ye unto the fruit of it when it yields the fruit and the ripening of it; Verily in this are signs for a people who believe.\nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ الْجِنَّ وَخَلَقَهُمْ وَخَرَقُوْا لَهٗ بَنِيْنَ وَبَنٰتٍۢ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(100)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A AL-JENNA WA KHALAQAHUM WAKHARAQOOA LAHU BANEENA WABANAATIN BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nAnd (yet) make they the jinn, the associates for God, while He created them, and they (foolishly) without knowledge assign to Him sons and daughters; Glory be to Him, and (the most) exalted is He, above what they attribute (unto Him).\nبَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّلَمْ تَكُنْ لَّهٗ صَاحِبَةٌ ؕ وَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ ۚ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(101)\nBADEE-U’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ ANNAA LAHUL LAHU WALADUN LAM TAKUN LAHU SAAHEBATUN WA KHALAQAL KULLA SHAY-IN WA HOWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\n(He is the) Originator of the heavens and the earth; How could He have an issue while He hath no consort; He created all things, He is the knower of all things.\nذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ فَاعْبُدُوْهُۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ‏(102)\nZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN FAAA’BUDOOHU WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\n(Behold Ye!) that is God, your Lord, there is no god but He, the Creator of all things, therefore worship Him and He over all things holds sway.\nلَا تُدْرِكُهُ الْاَبْصَارُ وَهُوَ يُدْرِكُ الْاَبْصَارَۚ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(103)\nLAA TUDREKUHU IZ ZAAGHATIL WA HOWA YUDREKU AL-AABSAARA WA HOWA LATEEFUL KHABEER.\nVision perceiveth Him not, and He perceiveth (all) vision; He is the Subtle, the All-Aware.\nقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَصَآئِرُ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْۚ فَمَنْ اَبْصَرَ فَلِنَفْسِهٖ ۚ وَمَنْ عَمِىَ فَعَلَيْهَا ؕ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَفِيْظٍ‏(104)\nQAD JAAA-AKUM BASAAERU MIN RABBEKUM FAMAN AABSARA FALENAFSEH WA MAN A’AMEAAA FA A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEHAFEEZIN.\nIndeed, have come unto you (clear) proofs from your Lord, whosoever therefore seest it, it is for his own self; and whosoever be (wilfully) blind then it is against him; I am not over you a keeper.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلِيَقُوْلُوْا دَرَسْتَ وَلِنُبَيِّنَهٗ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA KAZAALEKA NUSARREFU AAYAATE WALEEQOOLOOA DARASTA WALENUBAYNAH LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nAnd thus do We display the signs and that they may say “Thou hast been taught and that We may make it clear to people who know.\nاِتَّبِعْ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(106)\nAETTABEA’ MAA OOHEYA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WAAA’REZ A’NIL MUSHREKEEN.\nFollow thou what hath been revealed unto thee from thy Lord; There is no god but He, turn thee away from the polytheists.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكُوْا ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(107)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA ASHRAKOO WA MAA JAA’ALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nAnd had God (so) pleased, they would not have associated (others) with Him; and We have not made thee a keeper over them, nor art thou over them a guardian.\nوَلَا تَسُبُّوا الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَيَسُبُّوا اللّٰهَ عَدْوًاۢ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ زَيَّنَّا لِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ عَمَلَهُمْ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ مَّرْجِعُهُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(108)\nWA LAA TASUBBOOA LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAYASUBBOOA LAAHA A’ADWAN BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN KAZAALEKA ZAYYANNAA LEKULLIM UMMATIN A’AMALAHUM SUMMA ELAA RABBEHIM MMARJEU’UHUM FAYUNABBEUHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd abuse ye not those whom they invoke besides God, lest they abuse God in transgression without knowledge. Thus, have We made fair-seeming to every people their deeds, then unto their Lord is their return, so He will inform them of what they did.\nوَاَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ لَئِنْ جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيَةٌ لَّيُؤْمِنُنَّ بِهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا الْاٰيٰتُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَمَا يُشْعِرُكُمْۙ اَنَّهَاۤ اِذَا جَآءَتْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(109)\nWAAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAIL JAAA-AHUM TAA-TEENAA LLAYUMENUNNA BEHAA QUL INNAMAA AAYAATO I’NDAL LAAHE WA MAA YUSHE’ERUKUM AANNAHAA EZAA JAAA-AT LAA YOAMENOONA.\nAnd they swear by God with the strongest of their oaths that if came unto them a sign, they would most certainly believe in it; Say: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Verily signs are with God, but what should make ye know that when it cometh, they will not believe.\nوَنُقَلِّبُ اَفْئِدَتَهُمْ وَاَبْصَارَهُمْ كَمَا لَمْ يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهٖۤ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّنَذَرُهُمْ فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(110)\nWANUQALLEBU AAFEDATAHUM WAABSAARAHUM KAMAA LAM YOAMENOO BEHI AWWALA MARRAH WWANAZARUHUM FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nAnd We will turn (aside) their hearts and their visions, even as they did not believe in it the first time, and We will leave them in their contumacy, wandering blindly on.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّنَا نَزَّلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ وَكَلَّمَهُمُ الْمَوْتٰى وَ حَشَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ قُبُلًا مَّا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ يَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(111)\nWA LAW AANNANAA NAZZALNAA ELAYHEMUS AL-MALAAAEKATA WAKALLAMAHUMU MAWTAA WA HASHARNAA A’LAYHIM KULLA SHAY-IN QUBULAN MAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM YAJHALOONA.\nAnd had We sent down unto them the angels, and the dead had spoken to them and (even if) We had gathered all things before them, (even then) they would not believe unless that God (so) pleaseth but most of them (deliberately) ignore.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّا شَيٰطِيْنَ الْاِنْسِ وَالْجِنِّ يُوْحِىْ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍ زُخْرُفَ الْقَوْلِ غُرُوْرًا ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ مَا فَعَلُوْهُ فَذَرْهُمْ وَمَا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(112)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA LEKULLIM NABEAAAIN A’DUWWAL SHAYTEENA AL-AENSE WA JINNE YOOHEAA KHALAA ELAA ELAA ZUKHRUFA AL-QAWLE GHOROORAA WA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA MAA FAA’ALOOHU FAZARHUM WA MAA YAFTAROON.\nAnd thus did We make for every apostle an enemy, the devils from among men and jinn, inspire some of them unto the others tinsel discourses to deceive (them); and had thy Lord pleased they would not have done it, therefore leave them and what they forge.\nوَلِتَصْغٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَفْئِدَةُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ وَلِيَرْضَوْهُ وَلِيَقْتَرِفُوْا مَا هُمْ مُّقْتَرِفُوْنَ‏(113)\nWALETASGHAAA ELAYHE AAFEDATU LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WALEERZAWHU WALEEQTAREFOOA MAA HUM MMUQTAREFOONA.\nSo that, may incline unto it, the hearts of those who believe not in the (life) hereafter, so that they may be well pleased with it, and that they may earn what they do earn (of the evil).\nاَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْتَغِىْ حَكَمًا وَّهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ اِلَيْكُمُ الْكِتٰبَ مُفَصَّلاً ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهٗ مُنَزَّلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ بِالْحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَ‏(114)\nAAFAGHAYRA LAAHE AABTAGHEAA HAKAMAN WA LAZEE ANZALAL AELAYKUMU KETAABA MUFASSALAAN WAL LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YA’LAMOON ANNAHU MUNAZZALUN MIN RABBEKA BIL-HAQQE FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nShould other than God I seek a Judge, and when He it is Who hath sent down unto you the Book (the Qur’an) (fully) explained? And those whom We have given them the Book know that it hath been sent down from thy Lord with truth, so be thou not of those who doubt.\nوَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًا وَّعَدْلاً  ؕ لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمٰتِهٖ ۚ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(115)\nWATAMMAT KALEMATU RABBEKA SEDQAN WWAA’ADLAAN LAA MUBADDELA LEKALEMAATEH WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nAnd perfect is the word of thy Lord in truth and justice; There is none who can change His words, and He is the All-Hearing and the All Knowing.\nوَاِنْ تُطِعْ اَكْثَرَ مَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ يُضِلُّوْكَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(116)\nWA TO-TE’ AKSARAN MAN FIL ARZE YUZELLOOKA A’N SABEELIL LAAH IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA HUM ILLAA YAKHRUSOONA.\nAnd if thou obey most of those in the earth, they will lead thee astray from God’s way; they follow not but conjecture, they only (falsely) guess.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ مَنْ يَّضِلُّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖۚ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(117)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO MAN YYAZELLU A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nVerily, thy Lord, He knoweth best who strayeth away from His way, and knoweth best those who follow the right guidance.\nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(118)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA ZUKERA RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE IN KUNTUM BE-AAYAATEHI MUMENEENA.\nTherefore, eat ye (the meat) of that over which hath been mentioned the name of God, if ye be believers in His signs.\nوَمَا لَكُمْ اَلَّا تَاْكُلُوْا مِمَّا ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَقَدْ فَصَّلَ لَكُمْ مَّا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِلَّا مَا اضْطُرِرْتُمْ اِلَيْهِؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا لَّيُضِلُّوْنَ بِاَهْوَآئِهِمْ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(119)\nWA MAA LAKUM ALLAA TAAKULOOA MIMMAA ZUKERA RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE WA QAD FASSALA LAKUM MAA HARRAMA A’LAYKUM ILLAA MAA AZTURERTUM AELAYHE WA INNA KASEERAA LLAYUZELLOONA BEAAHWAAEHEM BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MO’TADEEN.\nAnd what hath happened to you that ye eat not (meat) of that over which hath been mentioned (Allah) the name of God, while He hath indeed made plain to you what He hath forbidden unto you, excepting what ye were compelled to; and many would lead people astray by their vain desires without knowledge; Verily, thy Lord knoweth best the transgressors.\nوَذَرُوْا ظَاهِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَبَاطِنَهٗؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ یَکْسِبُوْنَ الْاِثْمَ سَيُجْزَوْنَ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَقْتَرِفُوْنَ‏(120)\nWA ZAROO ZAAHERA AL-AESME WABAATENAH INNAL LAZEENA SEBOONA AL-AESMA SAYUJZAWNA BEMAA KAANOO YAQTAREFOONA.\nAnd leave ye, open and secret sins; verily those who earn sin, soon will they be recompensed with what they earned.\nوَلَا تَاْكُلُوْا مِمَّا لَمْ يُذْكَرِ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَاِنَّهٗ لَفِسْقٌ ؕ وَاِنَّ الشَّيٰطِيْنَ لَيُوْحُوْنَ اِلٰٓى اَوْلِيٰٓئِهِمْ لِيُجَادِلُوْكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ اَطَعْتُمُوْهُمْ اِنَّكُمْ لَمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(121)\nWA LAA TAAKULOOA MIMMAA LAM YUZKARE RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE WA INNAHU LAFESQUN WA INNA SHAYAATEENA LAYOOHOONA ELAA AAWLEEEHEM LEEJAADELOOKUM WA AATAA’TUMOOHUM INNAKUM LAMUSHREKOONA.\nAnd eat ye not of that on which God’s name (Allah) was not mentioned, while Verily it was transgression; and verily Satans inspire unto their friends, that they should contend with you, and if ye obey them, verily ye be polytheists.\nاَوَمَنْ كَانَ مَيْتًا فَاَحْيَيْنٰهُ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهٗ نُوْرًا يَّمْشِىْ بِهٖ فِى النَّاسِ كَمَنْ مَّثَلُهٗ فِى الظُّلُمٰتِ لَيْسَ بِخَارِجٍ مِّنْهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(122)\nAAWAMAN KAANA MAYTAN FAAHYAYNAAHU WA JA-A’LNAA LAHU NOORAN YAMSHEE BEHI FIL NAASE KAMAM MMASALUH FIL ZOLOMAATE LAYSA BEKHAAREJIN MINHAA KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LIL KAAFEREENA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nIs he who was dead, then We raised him to life and made for him a light by which he walketh among the people, like unto him whose similitude is that of one in utter darkness whence he cannot come forth? Thus hath been made fair seeming for the disbelievers what they did.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ قَرْيَةٍ اَكٰبِرَ مُجْرِمِيْهَا لِيَمْكُرُوْا فِيْهَا ؕ وَمَا يَمْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(123)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA FEE KULLE QARYATINW AAKAABERA MUJREMEEHAA LEEMKUROOA FEEHAA WA MAA YAMKOROON ILLAA BE-ANFOSEHIM WA MAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThus made We in every town great ones to be its guilty ones, that they may plot therein; and they plot not but against their own selves and they perceive not.\nوَاِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيَةٌ قَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ حَتّٰى نُؤْتٰى مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ رُسُلُ اللّٰهِؔۘؕ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ حَيْثُ يَجْعَلُ رِسٰلَتَهٗ ؕ سَيُصِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ اَجْرَمُوْا صَغَارٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AHUM TAA-TEENAA QAALOO LAN NOAMENA HATTAA NUTAA MISLA MAA OOTEYA RUSULU AL-LAAHE ALLAAHO A-A’LAMO HAYSO YAJA’ALU RESAALATAH SAYUSEEBU LAZEENA AJRAMOO SAGHAARUN I’NDAL LAAHE WA A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN BEMAA KAANOO YAMKOROON.\nAnd when cometh unto them a sign, they say: “Never will we believe until We are given the like of what was given unto the apostles of God,” God knoweth best where to place His apostleship: Soon shall befall those who are guilty, humiliation from God and severe chastisement for what they cunningly plot.\nفَمَنْ يُّرِدِ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّهْدِيَهٗ يَشْرَحْ صَدْرَهٗ لِلْاِسْلَامِۚ وَمَنْ يُّرِدْ اَنْ يُّضِلَّهٗ يَجْعَلْ صَدْرَهٗ ضَيِّقًا حَرَجًا كَاَنَّمَا يَصَّعَّدُ فِى السَّمَآءِؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَجْعَلُ اللّٰهُ الرِّجْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(125)\nFAMAN YYUREDE LAAHO AN YYAHDEEH YASHRAH SADRAH LIL-AESLAAME WA MAN YYURED AN YYUZELLAH YAJ-A’L SADRAH ZAYQAN HARAJAN KA-ANNAMAA YASSAAA’ADU FIL AS-SAMAAE KAZAALEKA YAJA’ALU LAAHO A’NKOMUR A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA.\nWhomsoever willeth God that He should guide him aright, He expandeth his breast for Islam, and whomsoever He intendeth to leave straying, He maketh his breast straitened and narrow as though he is climbing into the very skies. Thus, doth God layeth gnominious chastisement on those who believe not.\nوَهٰذَا صِرَاطُ رَبِّكَ مُسْتَقِيْمًا ؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(126)\nWA SERAATU RABBEKA MUSTAQEEMAN QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YYAZZAKKAROONA.\nAnd this is the path of thy Lord, a Straight path. Indeed, have We made clear the signs for the people who take heed.\nلَهُمْ دَارُ السَّلٰمِ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(127)\nLAHUM DAARU AS-SALAAME I’NDAL RABBEHIM WA HOWA WALEEHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nFor them shall be the abode of peace with their Lord, and He is their Guardian because of what they used to do.\nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ۚ يٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ قَدِ اسْتَكْثَرْتُمْ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِۚ وَقَالَ اَوْلِيٰٓئُهُمْ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِ رَبَّنَا اسْتَمْتَعَ بَعْضُنَا بِبَعْضٍ وَّبَلَغْنَاۤ اَجَلَنَا الَّذِىْۤ اَجَّلْتَ لَنَا ؕ قَالَ النَّارُ مَثْوٰٮكُمْ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(128)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A YAA JINNE QADE ASTAKSARTUM MENAL AL-AENSE WA QAALA AAWLEEUHUM MENAL AL-AENSE RABBANAA ASTAMTAA’A BAA’ZUNAA BE-BA’Z WWABALAGHNAA AAJALANAA LAZEE AAJJALTA LANAA QAALA TAMASSANAN MASWAAKUM KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ILLAA MAA SHAAA-ALLAAH INNAL RABBAKA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nAnd on the day when He shall gather them all together (and say): “O’ assembly of jinn! Ye increased your strength (by seducing a great number) from men;” And will say their friends among the men: “O’ Our Lord! Some of us profited by others and We have reached our term which Thou didst appoint for us;” He shall say. “The (Hell) fire is your abode, be ye the dwellers therein, save what pleaseth God; “Verily thy Lord is All-Wise, All-Knowing.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُوَلِّىْ بَعْضَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَعْضًاۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(129)\nWA KAZAALEKA NOOLLEAA YAWM ZAALEMEEN BA’ZAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nAnd thus do We make some of iniquitous to befriend the others because of what they earned.\nيٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ اَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَقُصُّوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْ وَيُنْذِرُوْنَكُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا ؕ قَالُوْا شَهِدْنَا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِنَا وَغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَشَهِدُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(130)\nYAA JINNE WAL INSE ALAM YAATEKUM RUSULUN MINKUM YAQUSSOONA A’LAYKUM AAAYAATEAA WAYUNZEROONAKUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA QAALOO SHAHIDNAA A’LAA AANFUSENAA WAGHARRATHUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA WASHAHEDOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM ANNAHUM KAANOO KAAFEREEN.\nO’ assembly of jinn and men! did not come unto you apostles from among you, relating to you My signs and warning you of the meeting of this day (of requital’) of yours?” They shall say: “We bear witness against Ourselves;” And this world’s life deceived them, and they shall bear witness against their (own) selves that they were disbelievers.\nذٰ لِكَ اَنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ رَّبُّكَ مُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى بِظُلْمٍ وَّاَهْلُهَا غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(131)\nZAA LEKA AN LAM YAKUL RRABBUKA MOHLEKAL KORAA BEZULMIN WWAAHLUHAA GHAAFELOON.\nThis because thy Lord destroyeth not any town un-justly whilst their occupants were negligent.\nوَلِكُلٍّ دَرَجٰتٌ مِّمَّا عَمِلُوْا ؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(132)\nWA DARAJAATUN MIMMAA A’MELOO WA MAA RABBOKA BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA YA’MALOON.\nAnd for all are degrees in accordance with what they do; and thy Lord is not heedless of what they do.\nوَرَبُّكَ الْغَنِىُّ ذُو الرَّحْمَةِ ؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ وَيَسْتَخْلِفْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِكُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُ كَمَاۤ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ قَوْمٍ اٰخَرِيْنَ ؕ‏(133)\nWA RABBOKA AL-GHANEAAAU ZUL AR-RAHMATE IN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM WAYASTAKHLEF MIN BAA’DEKUM MAA YASHAAA KAMAA AN-SHA-A MIN ZURREETE QAWMIN AAKHEREEN.\nAnd thy Lord is Self-Sufficient, full of Mercy; If He pleaseth He may take you away and make successors after you, whomsoever He pleaseth, even as He raised you up from the posterity of other people.\nاِنَّ مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَاٰتٍ ۙوَّمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(134)\nINNAL MAA TOO-A’DOON LAATIN WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nVerily what ye are promised, will certainly come to pass, and ye cannot make (God) helpless (against it).\nقُلْ يٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ مَنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(135)\nQUL LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN TAKOONO LAHU A’AQEBATUL DAAR INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nSay! “O’ My people! Act ye according to your ability; verily I too act, then soon will ye know for whom (of us) will be the abode of the (good) end (of bliss); Verily shall not succeed the unjust.\nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ مِمَّا ذَرَاَ مِنَ الْحَرْثِ وَالْاَنْعَامِ نَصِيْبًا فَقَالُوْا هٰذَا لِلّٰهِ بِزَعْمِهِمْ وَهٰذَا لِشُرَكَآئِنَا ۚ فَمَا كَانَ لِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ فَلَا يَصِلُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ لِلّٰهِ فَهُوَ يَصِلُ اِلٰى شُرَكَآئِهِمْ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(136)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE MIMMAA ZARAA MENAL AL-HARSE WAL AANA’AAME NASEEBAN FA-QAALOO HAAZAA LILLAAHE BEZAA’MEHEM WA LESHURAKAAENAA FAMAA KAANA LE-SHORAKAAA-EHIM FALAA YASELU ELAL LAAHE WA MAA KAANA LILLAAHE FAHOWA YASELU ELAA SHORAKAAA-EHIM SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nThey assign unto God from what He hath created of tilth and cattle, and say: “This is for God, according to their assertion, and this for our associates, then what is for their associates reacheth not unto God, and whatever be for God, it reacheth their associates; (How) evil is what they judge!\nوَكَذٰلِكَ زَيَّنَ لِكَثِيْرٍ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ قَتْلَ اَوْلَادِهِمْ شُرَكَآؤُهُمْ لِيُرْدُوْهُمْ وَلِيَلْبِسُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ دِيْنَهُمْ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا فَعَلُوْهُ ؕ فَذَرْهُمْ وَمَا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(137)\nWA KAZAALEKA ZAYNA LE-KASEERIM MENAL MUSHREKEEN QATLA AAWLAADEHEM SHURAKAAUHUM LEERDOOHUM WALEELBESOOA A’LAYHIM DEENAHUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA FAA’ALOOHU FAZARHUM WA MAA YAFTAROON.\nAnd thus their “Associates have made fair-seeming to most of the polytheists the slaying of their (own) children that they may cause them to perish, and confound unto them their religion, and if God hath desired they would not have done so, therefore leave them and what they forge.\nوَقَالُوْا هٰذِهٖۤ اَنْعَامٌ وَّحَرْثٌ حِجْرٌ ۖ لَّا يَطْعَمُهَاۤ اِلَّا مَنْ نَّشَآءُ بِزَعْمِهِمْ وَاَنْعَامٌ حُرِّمَتْ ظُهُوْرُهَا وَاَنْعَامٌ لَّا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهَا افْتِرَآءً عَلَيْهِ ؕ سَيَجْزِيْهِمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(138)\nWA QAALOO HAAZEHI AANA’AAMUN WWAHARSUN HEJRUN LAA YATA’AMUHAA ILLAA MAN NNASHAAU BEZAA’MEHEM WAANA’AAMUN HURREMAT ZUHOORUHAA WAANA’AAMUN LAA YAZKUROONA KORISMA LAAHE A’LAYHAA AFTERAAAN A’LAYHE SAYAJZEEHEM BEMAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd say they: “These cattle and tilth are a taboo (consecrated): None shall eat them save as we please” (this is) according to their own Assertion, and (there are) cattle whose backs are forbidden and cattle they mention not (Allah) God’s name on them-forging a lie against Him, soon will He requite them for what they forge.\nوَقَالُوْا مَا فِىْ بُطُوْنِ هٰذِهِ الْاَنْعَامِ خَالِصَةٌ لِّذُكُوْرِنَا وَمُحَرَّمٌ عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِنَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مَّيْتَةً فَهُمْ فِيْهِ شُرَكَآءُ ؕ سَيَجْزِيْهِمْ وَصْفَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(139)\nWA QAALOO MAA FEE BUTOONE HAAZEHE AL-AANA’AAME KHAALESATUN LLEZUKOORENAA WA MOHARRAMUM A’LAA AAZWAAJENAA WA YYAKUN MMAYTATAN FAHUM FEEHE SHURAKAAU SAYAJZEEHEM WASFAHUM INNAHU HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nAnd they say: “What is in the wombs of these cattle is exclusively for our males and forbidden to our wives and if it be still born, then all of them, in it are partners;” soon will He recompense them for (falsely) attributing to God; Verily He is All-Wise, All-Knowing.\nقَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَتَلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَهُمْ سَفَهًۢا بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّحَرَّمُوْا مَا رَزَقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ افْتِرَآءً عَلَى اللّٰهِؕ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا وَمَا كَانُوْا مُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(140)\nQAD KHASERA LAZEENA QATALOOA AAWLAADAHUM SAFAHAN BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WWAHARRAMOOA MAA RAZAQAHUMU LAAHO AFTERAAAN A’LAL LAAH QAD ZALLOOA WA MAA KAANOO MOHTADEEN.\nIndeed, are lost those who slay their children foolishly without knowledge and prohibit they what God hath given them, forging falsehood against God. Indeed, they have gone astray and they are not guided aright.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَ جَنّٰتٍ مَّعْرُوْشٰتٍ وَّغَيْرَ مَعْرُوْشٰتٍ وَّالنَّخْلَ وَالزَّرْعَ مُخْتَلِفًا اُكُلُهٗ وَالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالرُّمَّانَ مُتَشَابِهًا وَّغَيْرَ مُتَشَابِهٍ ؕ كُلُوْا مِنْ ثَمَرِهٖۤ اِذَاۤ اَثْمَرَ وَاٰتُوْا حَقَّهٗ يَوْمَ حَصَادِهٖ ۖ وَلَا تُسْرِفُوْا ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(141)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AANSHAA JANNAATIN MMAA’ROOSHAATIN WWAGHAYRA MAA’ROOSHAATIN WWAALNNAKHLA WAALZZARA’A MUKHTALEFAN AUKULUH WAALZZAYTOONA WAALRRUMMAANA MOTASHAA-BEHAA WWAGHAYRA MUTASHAABEHIN KOLOO MIN SAMAREHI EZAA AASMARA WAATOOA HAQQAHU YAWMA HASAADEH WA LAA TUSREFOOA INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL MUSREFEEN.\nAnd He it is who produceth gardens (of vine) trellised and untrellised, and date palms and tilth of various (kinds of food produce) and olives and pomegranates, similar (in kind) and different (in variety), eat ye of its fruit when it fruiteth and give ye His (God’s) share, on the day of its reaping, and act ye not extravagantly; Verily He loveth not the extravagant (ones).\nوَ مِنَ الْاَنْعَامِ حَمُوْلَةً وَّفَرْشًا ؕ كُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَ لَا تَتَّبِعُوْا خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ ۙ‏(142)\nWA MENAL AL-AANA’AAME HAMOOLATAN WWAFARSHAN KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABE-O’O KHOTOWATIS SHAYTAANE INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nAnd of cattle are some bearers of burden and some (low fit only) for spreading; eat ye of what God provideth you with, and follow ye not the footsteps of Satan; verily he is your declared enemy.\nثَمٰنِيَةَ اَزْوَاجٍ ۚ مِنَ الضَّاْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْمَعْزِ اثْنَيْنِ ؕ قُلْ ءٰٓالذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ اَمِ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ اَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ اَرْحَامُ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ نَبِّئُوْنِىْ بِعِلْمٍ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ ۙ‏(143)\nSAMAANEETA AZWAAJINW MENAL AZ-ZAANE NAYNE WA MENAN AL-MAA’ZE NAYNE QUL AAALZZAKARAYNE HARRAMA AMIL AL-AUNSAYAYNE AMMAA ASHTAMALAT A’LAYHE AARHAAMU AL-AUNSAYAYNE NABBEOONEAA BE-I’LMIN IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\n(Take) Eight in pairs-two of sheep and two of goats; Say: “Hath He forbidden the two males or the two females or what is contained in the wombs of the two females? Inform me with knowledge, if ye be truthful.\nوَمِنَ الْاِبِلِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ اثْنَيْنِ ؕ قُلْ ءٰٓالذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ اَمِ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ اَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ اَرْحَامُ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ اَمْ كُنْتُمْ شُهَدَآءَ اِذْ وَصّٰٮكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا ۚ فَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا لِّيُضِلَّ النَّاسَ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(144)\nWA MENAN AL-AEBELE NAYNE WA MENAN AL-BAQARE NAYNE QUL AAALZZAKARAYNE HARRAMA AMIL AL-AUNSAYAYNE AMMAA ASHTAMALAT A’LAYHE AARHAAMU AL-AUNSAYAYNE AM KUNTUM SHOHADAAA-A IZ WASSAAKUMU LAAHO BEHAAZAA FAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN LLEEZELLA NAASA BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd of the two camels and of the two oxen; say, the two males hath He forbidden or the two females or that which contain the (wombs) of the two females? or were ye witnesses when God did enjoin this;” Who, then is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God to lead astray mankind without knowledge? Verily guideth not God a people who are unjust.\nقُل لَّاۤ اَجِدُ فِىْ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ مُحَرَّمًا عَلٰى طَاعِمٍ يَّطْعَمُهٗۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مَيْتَةً اَوْ دَمًا مَّسْفُوْحًا اَوْ لَحْمَ خِنْزِيْرٍ فَاِنَّهٗ رِجْسٌ اَوْ فِسْقًا اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖۚ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ بَاغٍ وَّلَا عَادٍ فَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(145)\nQUL LAA AAJEDU FEE MAA OOHEYA ELAYYA MUHARRAMAN A’LAA TAAE’EMIN YYATA’AMUH ILLAA AN YAKOONA MAYTATAN AW DAMAN MMASFOOHAN AW LAHMA KHENZEERIN FA-INNAHU REJSUN AW FESQAN OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI FAMANE’ TURRA GHAYRA BAAGHINW WA LAA A’ADIN FA-INNAL RABBAKA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSay: “I find not in what hath been revealed unto me anything forbidden to an eater to eat except it be died of itself, or blood poured forth or flesh of swine for verily that is unclean or a transgression,(a) slain invoking the name of other than Allah (God), but (even so) if one is forced (to eat it) not lusting nor (wilfully) transgressing the limits, then verily thy Lord is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nوَعَلَى الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا كُلَّ ذِىْ ظُفُرٍ ۚ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ وَالْغَنَمِ حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ شُحُوْمَهُمَاۤ اِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتْ ظُهُوْرُهُمَاۤ اَوِ الْحَوَايَاۤ اَوْ مَا اخْتَلَطَ بِعَظْمٍ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ جَزَيْنٰهُمْ بِبَغْيِهِمْ ۖ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(146)\nWA LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA KULLA ZEE ZUFURIN WA MENAN AL-BAQARE WAL GHANAME HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIM SHUHOOMAHUMAA ILLAA MAA HAMALAT ZUHOORUHUMAA AWE’ AL-HAWAAYAA AW MAA AKHTALATA BEA’AZMIN ZAA LEKA JAZAYNAAHUM BEBAGHYEHEM WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\nAnd unto those who were Jews forbade We every animal having undivided hoof, and of oxen and sheep forbade We unto them the fat of both, save what is upon their backs or the entrails or what is mixed with bones; this We recompensed them for their rebellion, and verily We are truthful.\nفَاِنْ كَذَّبُوْكَ فَقُلْ رَّبُّكُمْ ذُوْ رَحْمَةٍ وَّاسِعَةٍ ۚ وَلَا يُرَدُّ بَاْسُهٗ عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(147)\nFA-IN KAZZABOOKA FAQUL RRABBUKUM ZOO RAHMATIN WWAASEA’ATIN WA LAA YORADDO BAASUH A’NIL QAWMIL MUJREMEEN.\nIf they belie thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) then say (though) “thy Lord is full of Mercy all-embracing but His wrath shall not be returned from the people who are guilty.\nسَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكْنَا وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمْنَا مِنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ حَتّٰى ذَاقُوْا بَاْسَنَا ؕ قُلْ هَلْ عِنْدَكُمْ مِّنْ عِلْمٍ فَتُخْرِجُوْهُ لَنَا ؕ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا تَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(148)\nSA-YAQOOLO LAZEENA ASHRAKOO LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA AASHRAKNAA WA LAA AAABAAUNAA WA LAA HARRAMNAA MIN SHAY-IN KAZAALEKA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM HATTAA ZAAQOO BAASANAA QUL HAL E’ENDAKUM MIN I’LMIN FATUKHREJOOHU LANAA IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA ANTUM ILLAA TAKHRUSOONA.\nThose who are polytheists will say: “Had God wished we would not have associated (aught with Him) nor our fathers, nor would we have forbidden (to ourselves) anything.” So did belie those before them until they tested Our wrath; Say thou: “Have ye with you any knowledge? Then produce ye that unto us, ye follow naught but conjecture and ye utter naught but guessing.\nقُلْ فَلِلّٰهِ الْحُجَّةُ الْبَالِغَةُ ۚ فَلَوْ شَآءَ لَهَدٰٮكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(149)\nQUL FALILLAAHE AL-HUJJATU AL-BAALEGHATU FA LAW SHAAA-AL LAHADAAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nSay thou: “Then, God’s (alone) is the argument decisive; Had God wished He would surely have guided you all aright.\nقُلْ هَلُمَّ شُهَدَآءَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ يَشْهَدُوْنَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ حَرَّمَ هٰذَا ۚ فَاِنْ شَهِدُوْا فَلَا تَشْهَدْ مَعَهُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ وَهُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(150)\nQUL HALUMMA SHUHADAAAKUMU LAZEENA YASHHADOONA ANNAL LAAHA HARRAMA HAAZAA FA-IN SHAHEDOOA FALAA TASHHAD MA-A’HUM WA LAA TATTABEA’ AAHWAAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WA HUM BE-RABBEHIM YAA’DELOONA.\nSay thou: “Bring ye your witnesses who bear witness that God hath forbidden this,” then (even) if they bear witness, bear thou not witness with them; and follow not thou the inclinations of those who belie Our signs; and those who believe not in the hereafter, and while they with their Lord equalize (others).\nقُلْ تَعَالَوْا اَتْلُ مَا حَرَّمَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ اَلَّا تُشْرِكُوْا بِهٖ شَيْئًا وَّبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَكُمْ مِّنْ اِمْلَاقٍؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكُمْ وَاِيَّاهُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(151)\nQUL TA-A’ALAW AATLU MAA HARRAMA RABBOKUM A’LAYKUM ALLAA TUSHREKOOA BEHI SHAY-ANW WWABEALWAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW WA LAA TAQTULOOA AWLAADAKUM MIN AEMLAAQIN NAHNO NARZUQUKUM WAAYYAAHUM WA LAA TAQRABOOA AL-FAWAAHESHA MAA ZAHARAL MINHAA WA MAA BATANA WA LAA TAQTULOOA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) “Come ye! I will recite (unto) you what your Lord hath forbidden to you that ye associate not with Him anything and to ( your) parents be good, and slay ye not your children for (fear of) poverty; We provide for you and for them, and draw ye not near unto shameful deeds, that which be apparent and that which be concealed, and kill ye not the soul which God hath forbidden save for justice; This He enjoineth you with, so that ye may understand.\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوْا مَالَ الْيَتِيْمِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ اَشُدَّهٗ ۚ وَاَوْفُوْا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ ۚ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ وَاِذَا قُلْتُمْ فَاعْدِلُوْا وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبٰى ۚ وَبِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ اَوْفُوْا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ ۙ‏(152)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA MAALA AL-YATEEME ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO HATTAA HATTAA ASHUDDAHU WA AWFOO AL-KAYLA WA MEEZAAN BIL QISTE LAA NUKALLEFU NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA WA EZAA IZ QULTUM FAAA’DELOOA WA LAW KAANA ZAL QURBAA WABEA’AHDE LAAHE AAWFOOA ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nAnd approach ye not the property of an orphan save that be in the best manner till he attaineth his maturity; Give ye full measure and full weight in (perfect) justice; We task not a soul but according to his ability, and when ye speak be just; though it be against a kinsman; and fulfil ye God’s covenant; This He enjoineth you with so that ye may be mindful.\nوَاَنَّ هٰذَا صِرَاطِىْ مُسْتَقِيْمًا فَاتَّبِعُوْهُ ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا السُّبُلَ فَتَفَرَّقَ بِكُمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(153)\nWA ANNAL HAAZAA SERAATEAA MUSTAQEEMAN FAATTABEU’OOHU WA LAA TATTABE-O’O AS-SUBULA FA MAA BEKUM A’N SABEELEH ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOON.\nAnd (know ye) Verily this My path, is the straight (right) one, so ye follow it, and follow ye not (other) ways for they will scatter you away from His path; this doth He enjoin you with, so that ye may guard (yourselves against evil).\nثُمَّ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ تَمَامًا عَلَى الَّذِىْۤ اَحْسَنَ وَتَفْصِيْلاً لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُدًى وَرَحْمَةً لَّعَلَّهُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(154)\nSUMMA AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA TAMAAMAN A’LAL LAZEE AHSANAL WATAFSEELAAN LEKULLE SHAY-IN WWAHUDAN WA RAHMATAM LA-A’LLAHUM BELEQAAE RABBEHIM YOAMENOONA.\nBesides, We gave Moses the Book completing (our favours) on those who would do good and explaining all things in details, and a guidance and a mercy, so that in the meeting of their Lord they may believe.\nوَهٰذَا كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مُبٰرَكٌ فَاتَّبِعُوْهُ وَاتَّقُوْا لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَۙ‏(155)\nWA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO MUBAARAKUN FAATTABEU’OOHU WAT TAQOO LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nAnd this (Qur’an) is a Book, We have sent it down, blessed, so follow it, and guard (your-selves against evil) so that ye may be done mercy.\nاَنْ تَقُوْلُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ الْكِتٰبُ عَلٰى طَآئِفَتَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا وَاِنْ كُنَّا عَنْ دِرَاسَتِهِمْ لَغٰفِلِيْنَۙ‏(156)\nAN TAQOOLOO INNAMAA UNZELA KETAABO A’LAA TAAEFATAYNE MIN LAA WA KUNNAA A’N DERAASATEHEM LAGHAAFELEENA.\nLest ye (Polytheists) should say “that the Book (from God) was sent down unto two parties (the Christians and the Jews) before us, and verily we were of what they read, unaware.\nاَوْ تَقُوْلُوْا لَوْ اَنَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْكِتٰبُ لَكُنَّاۤ اَهْدٰى مِنْهُمْ ۚ فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ  ۚ فَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَصَدَفَ عَنْهَا ؕ سَنَجْزِى الَّذِيْنَ يَصْدِفُوْنَ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْدِفُوْنَ‏(157)\nAW TAQOOLOO LAW ANNAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA KETAABO LAKUNNAA AHDAA MINHUM FAQAD JAAA-AKUM BAYNATUN MIN RABBEKUM WA HODANW WA RAHMAH FAMAN AZLAMO MIMMAN KAZZABA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WASADAFA A’NHAA SA-NAJZIL LAZEENA YASDEFOONA A’N AAYAATENAA SOOO-AL A’ZAABE BEMAA KAANOO YASDEFOONA.\nOr (lest) ye should say: “Had only been sent unto us a book we should have been better guided than they;” so indeed hath (now) come unto you a manifest proof from your Lord, and guidance and mercy; who then is more unjust than he who belieth the signs of God and turneth away from them? Soon shall We recompense those who turn away from Our signs with an evil chastisement for what they used to turn away.\nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ رَبُّكَ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ بَعْضُ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكَ ؕ يَوْمَ يَاْتِىْ بَعْضُ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكَ لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا اِيْمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ اٰمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ اَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِىْۤ اِيْمَانِهَا خَيْرًا ؕ قُلِ انْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنَّا مُنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(158)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA AN TAA-TEYAHOMUL AL-MALAAEKATU AW HATTAA RABBOKA AW HATTAA BA’ZUL AAYAATIL RABBEKA YAWMA YAATEE BA’ZUL AAYAATIL RABBEKA LAA YANFAU’N NAFSAN AEEMAANUHAA LAM TAKUN AAAMANAT MIN QABLO AW KASABAT FEE AEEMAANEHAA KHAYRAN QOLIL ANTAZEROOA INNAA MUNTAZEROONA.\nThey wait not but (to see) that come unto them the angels, or cometh thy Lord (Himself), or that come (unto them) some signs of thy Lord; on the day when come some of the signs of thy Lord, its faith shall profit not a soul which believed not before, or earned good through its faith; Say: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) “Wait ye! Verily We too are waiting.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ فَرَّقُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ وَكَانُوْا شِيَعًا لَّسْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِىْ شَىْءٍ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَمْرُهُمْ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(159)\nINNAL LAZEENA FARRAQOO DEENAHUM WA KAANOO AHLAHAA LLASTA MINHUM FEE SHAY-IN INNAMAA AAMRUHUM ELAL LAAHE SUMMA YUNABBEUHUM BEMAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nVerily those who divided their religion and became parties, thou hast no concern with anything of them; their affair is with God only, then will He inform them of what they did.\nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ عَشْرُ اَمْثَالِهَا ۚ وَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزٰٓى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(160)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL-HASANATE FALAHU A’ASHRU AAMSAALEHAA WA MAN JAAA-A BIS-SAYYEATE FALAA YUJZAAA ILLAA MESLAHAA WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nWhosoever cometh with a good (deed) for him shall be ten like it; and whosoever cometh with an evil (deed) he shall be recompensed not but with the like of it, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.\nقُلْ اِنَّنِىْ هَدٰٮنِىْ رَبِّىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍۚ دِيْنًا قِيَمًا مِّلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا ۚ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(161)\nQUL INNANEE HADAANEAA RABBEE ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM DEENAN QEEMAN MMELLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) “Verily my Lord hath guided me unto the straight (right) path; the established religion, the faith of Abraham, the upright one; and he was not of the polytheists.\nقُلْ اِنَّ صَلَاتِىْ وَنُسُكِىْ وَ مَحْيَاىَ وَمَمَاتِىْ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(162)\nQUL INNAL SALAATEAA WANUSUKEAA WA MAHYAAAAA WAMAMAATEAA LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nSay: “Verily my prayer and my sacrifice, my life and my death, (are all, only) for God, the Lord of the worlds.\nلَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗۚ وَبِذٰلِكَ اُمِرْتُ وَاَنَا اَوَّلُ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(163)\nLAA SHAREEKA LAHU WABEZAALEKA AN A-A’BODA ANAT AAWLU AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nNo associate (is there) for Him; and this I am commanded, I am the first of the Muslims (i.e., those who submit to God).\nقُلْ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْغِىْ رَبًّا وَّهُوَ رَبُّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ ؕ وَلَا تَكْسِبُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ اِلَّا عَلَيْهَاۚ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى ۚ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ مَّرْجِعُكُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(164)\nQUL AAGHAYRA LAAHE AABGHEAA RABBAN WA RABBUL KULLE SHAY-IN WA LAA TAKSEBU KULLO NAFSIM ILLAA A’LAYHAA WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM MMARJEU’UKUM FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nSay: “Shall I seek other than God a Lord? While He is the Lord of all things; and no soul earneth (any evil deed) but against itself; and no bearer of burden shall bear the burden of another; then unto your Lord is your return, so He will inform you of what ye used to differ (about)\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَكُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ الْاَرْضِ وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَكُمْ فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ دَرَجٰتٍ لِّيَبْلُوَكُمْ فِىْ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ سَرِيْعُ الْعِقَابِ  ۖ وَاِنَّهٗ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(165)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JAA’ALAKUM KHALAAAEFA ARZE RA-FA-A’ BAA’ZAKUM FAWQA ELAA DARAJAATIN LLEEBLOOKUM FEE MAA AAATAAKUM INNAL RABBAKA SAREE-U’L E’QAAB WA INNAHU LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nAnd He it is who hath made you (His) Vicegerent in the earth and raised some of you above others in grades, that He may try you in what He gave you; Verily thy Lord is quick in the requital (of evil) and (yet) verily He is the Oft-Forgiving, the Merciful.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and contains a total of 165 verses. Imam Reza (a.s.) has said that this Surah was revealed accompanied by the descending of seventy thousand angels. These angels will ask forgiveness from Allah (s.w.t.) for any person who recites this Surah, and they will continue doing so until the Day of Judgement.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person writes this Surah using musk or saffron and then drinks it (ie. puts the written Surah in water for its writing to dissolve) for six consecutive days, that person will be blessed abundantly and will be free from all problems and ailments. He will not loose his health or fall sick.\nThe 6th Holy Imam (a.s.) also said that this Surah must be accorded due respect as the name of Allah (s.w.t.) appears 70 times in it. If people knew the benefits of reciting this Surah, they would never leave it."
}
